license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  AlgoPlasma, formerly the Plasma Modeling Subprogram Library (PMSL),
  is an open-source collection of reusable numerical algorithms for
  plasma modeling. Its source-level components cover particle
  initialization and advancement, particle-grid coupling, Poisson and
  Maxwell solvers, collision models, selected continuity updates,
  parallel data exchange, and input/output. Users select and compile
  components within application-specific programs, retaining control
  over data structures, physical coupling, boundary conditions, and
  execution order. Documentation links numerical formulations to source
  interfaces and usage, while available verification and validation
  cases support independent assessment. MPI routines provide
  distributed-memory communication, and selected computational kernels
  use OpenMP for shared-memory parallelism. The collection supports
  plasma-modeling research, numerical verification, and education.
keywords:
  - plasma modeling
  - numerical algorithms
  - particle-in-cell
  - parallel computing
  - verification and validation
  - scientific software
